WEBVTT

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:10.430
During the mild climate between autumn and winter,

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.500
the students of Queen's Academy

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:17.860
use the new train branch to go
back to Carmody every Friday.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.250
There, Diana and her friends pick them
up at the train station,

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.990
and they happily walk to Avonlea in the evening.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.460
Welcome home, Josie.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.200
Welcome back, Ruby.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.190
Gilbert!

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.220
Welcome back, Anne!

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.690
Diana!

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.230
Anne, you look well.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.190
So do you.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.960
Let me take your bag.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:50.720
No need.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:51.540
- Ow!
- Ow!

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.920
Matthew! Please calm down
and stop pacing around.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.980
Anne's train has probably
just reached Carmody.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:23.230
Anne won't come back any earlier
no matter how much you pace around.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.340
Well, now...

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.580
That's true.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:29.810
Ouch!

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.900
It would seem that you're not that calm yourself.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:38.720
I'm just thinking that maybe Anne
will be hungry when she's back.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:42.520
I have to get dinner ready so she can
dig right in when she's back home.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.220
This is getting worse.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:46.950
What did you say?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.380
Nothing. I didn't say a word.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.090
So, do Ruby wear her hair up?

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.150
Yes, in town.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:11.620
But it's a secret.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:15.270
But she has to take it down
when she comes home,

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.250
so her mother won't find
out and give her a scolding.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.480
I would have wanted to see that.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:20.850
It's like this.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.490
Are those two like that all the time in town?

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.890
For now, anyway.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:31.130
But Ruby isn't the sort of girl Gilbert likes.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:31.880
Right, Anne?

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.000
Huh? Well...

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:38.410
But Ruby's pretty, and Gilbert's handsome.
They might fit each other.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:39.480
Right.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:44.440
But Ruby told us that she can't
understand half of what Gilbert's saying

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.920
And when Gil is lost in thought, he starts
talking the way you tend to do.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.890
But Ruby, whether it's about
books or anything else,

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.560
doesn't like to use her
head when it's unnecessary.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.530
Frank Stockley is much more active,

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.750
but he's not half as handsome as Gilbert,

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.160
so she can't make up her
mind who she really likes.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.030
Ruby's starting to grow up.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.930
Yep. She's going according to her plan.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.400
That's not true.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:15.810
Oh, really?

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.370
Yes!

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.910
Though Anne says that...

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:23.850
she doesn't think Ruby
really is Gilbert's girlfriend.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:26.920
And Anne thinks that if she could be friends with Gilbert,

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.040
they would be able to joke,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:33.460
exchange opinions on books
and studying in the future.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.810
She cannot help but think that
it would be fun and wonderful.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.330
Well, we've come to the house at last.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:52.490
That's quite all right.

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.710
This has been the best time I've had this week.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.870
Well, this time I will accompany
you to the bridge over the brook.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.980
Matthew and Marilla are waiting for you.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.460
It's fine. I still have some things to tell you.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.690
You're such a bad girl.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:14.500
Anne has finally come back together with Diana.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.760
Oh, Anne...

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:30.580
I haven't told anyone else about this.
I want to confide in you alone.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:35.820
This time, Queen Academy is going to
get one of the Avery scholarships.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:38.050
One can go to a college on
the mainland free of charge.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:42.710
However, it's difficult, since only one
of the graduates can receive it.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.330
I understand! You're aiming for that, don't you?

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.230
Yes.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.300
That's amazing!

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:51.300
A gold medal and a scholarship.
You're quite ambitious, aren't you?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.340
But having a goal for your
studies is a good thing, isn't it?

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.660
Even if you fail.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:57.890
Of course!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.070
If you get it, could you get a bachelor's degree?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.980
But college lasts for four years, right?

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.050
I'm going to be lonely
if you're away during that time.

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.300
That's true.

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:13.300
That's why I haven't told
Matthew and Marilla about it yet.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:17.240
They expect me to come back
to Green Gables next year

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.330
and become a teacher at the school.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.670
Somehow, I feel a bit sorry.

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:28.770
But getting the Avery scholarship
is a great honor, isn't it?

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.750
Then there's no problem!
I'm sure Matthew will be all for it!

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:35.600
You think so?

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.390
Of course, and it's free of charge!

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:41.370
He's was delighted when you
got into Queen's, after all.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:45.020
I'm sure Marilla won't be opposed
to you getting a bachelor's degree.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.510
That may be so.

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:49.990
Anyway, you've given me courage.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:53.130
It will be all right. Give it your all, Anne.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:58.500
Thank you, Diana. Thanks to your
encouragement, I am reassured.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.340
I will always believe in you.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:02.900
Diana...

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:11.170
Oh, Anne. I wonder how long she's going
to stand there and chat with Diana.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.680
She could invite Diana into the house.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:18.120
And Matthew here said he was so eager
to see her a little while ago.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:19.910
Well, now...

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:23.600
I think they have a lot to talk about.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:24.970
So...

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.830
I know that!

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:29.560
Ah! She's coming. She's coming back!

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.310
I'm home!

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.010
I'm home, Matthew and Marilla!

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.380
Welcome back.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.890
Well! So you've come back?

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:44.920
Welcome back.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:50.950
Oh! This is the smell of Green Gables
that I've missed so much.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.460
Oh, it's just the ordinary smell of cooking.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.500
Are you hungry?

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:56.220
Yes.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.470
Dinner's ready.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.830
We will eat as soon as
you have washed your hands.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.840
Yes! I had forgotten about hunger, because
I was so happy to be back home.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.490
I'm actually starving!

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.620
Don't you mean you were happy to see Diana?

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:13.480
Huh?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:18.190
Oh, nothing. I thought you would be hungry,
so I made a feast for you tonight.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:21.350
You must eat a lot, now that you're home.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:24.550
Thank you, Marilla. I'll go change immediately.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:25.450
Hurry up!

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.890
I will!

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.220
This is for you, Marilla. It's a scarf.

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:44.180
It was very cheap, so it was a bargain.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:47.770
I found it in town, and thought
it would be just right for you.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.180
Do you like it?

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:54.960
It's not gaudy and I like the pattern. Thank you.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:59.980
I've was thinking of getting you a present, Matthew,

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.300
but I really didn't know
what to get for you.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:03.950
I'm sorry.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:10.970
That you come home every
week is the best present for me, Anne.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:17.210
But you know, Anne, while I'm not
going to find fault with a present,

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.590
I want you to use your money with care.

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.680
Though our livelihood isn't in trouble,
I don't want you to be wasteful.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:28.420
It's fine, Marilla. She doesn't do it often.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:31.750
No. It's best to be frank at a time like this.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:36.740
As soon as I saw that scarf, I thought
it would be perfect for you, Marilla.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.700
But I understand what you mean.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.300
I will be careful.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:45.630
I'm not angry with you.
Actually, I'm rather happy.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:48.300
If you will be more careful
from now on, then it's fine.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:49.960
Now, eat before it gets cold.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.210
Thank you.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.840
Oh, it looks delicious!
Thank you for the food!

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.700
So how's school life?

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.760
I've told you about Priscilla Grant, right?

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:21.140
Yes, that girl who's always
imagining things, just like you?

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:21.850
Well!

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:27.370
Now that we've become friends,
I've found that she's quite intellectual.

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:29.860
She's very playful and jokes a lot.

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:32.600
But I like Stella Maynard best.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.120
She has dark eyes, but she
has a really bright personality.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:40.730
Of course she ranks behind Diana.
Diana will always be my best friend.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.730
How are you doing in school?

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:47.500
I think that it's going smoothly for now.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.030
Then you will be able to pass
the graduation exam next year

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:53.100
and become a teacher, won't you?

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.630
Y-Yes.

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.790
That's reassuring to know, isn't it, Matthew?

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:58.770
Yes.

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:00.580
Is everything fine with Gilbert Blythe?

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:04.570
Well... Gilbert is doing great.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.380
He's studying with the
gold medal as a goal.

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.780
He's a formidable adversary as usual.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:13.400
No, Anne. He can't match you.

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:15.900
Matthew, you shouldn't say such things.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.270
Please don't make Anne
exert herself too much.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.890
Well, now...

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.030
Just make sure you stay healthy.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.100
Don't worry. Can I eat now?

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.230
I still haven't...

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:30.910
It's all because you ask so many questions.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.920
You're right about that!
Go ahead and eat!

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:37.310
Sorry.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:43.520
While Anne's growing up,
Matthew and Marilla are growing old.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:48.590
While coming home to Green Gables
once every week is a delight to Anne,

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:54.260
to Matthew and Marilla, it is the
joy which is the center of their lives.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:32.980
Good morning, Marilla.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:34.970
Oh, you're up this early?

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:37.460
It's fine if you take it easy on
the days you come home.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.800
It wouldn't do if I slept till late
when I'm at Green Gables.

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:44.510
Let's go milk the cows.
You'll be surprised.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.080
Really?!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:48.780
Oh yes! The bucket!

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.160
What's the hurry?

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.680
It's been born, hasn't it?

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:57.310
Well, well.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.960
Oh! It really has been born!

00:14:14.050 --> 00:14:15.270
It's so cute!

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:25.960
Good morning, Anne.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:27.390
Good morning, Matthew.

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.930
Calves are so cute.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.450
It was born last Tuesday morning.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.560
It belongs to you.

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:36.760
What?

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:40.700
Well... I'm giving it to you.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.670
Really?!

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:44.940
Oh! Thank you, Matthew!

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:48.020
What a wonderful present! But...

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:54.400
I'll take care of it for you,
but you are its master.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.650
About it's name...

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:01.500
Wait.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:06.210
Well, I think you should name it.
It hasn't got one yet.

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.090
That's great!

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:13.770
I'll call it Dolly.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.460
Because its dark eyes sparkle,
and it seems to be very demure.

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:19.310
So it's Dolly?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:26.440
Come here.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.690
Good morning. You're all fine, right?

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.440
On her weekend vacation,

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:45.580
Anne does the same things as when
she was going to school in Avonlea.

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:50.840
She helps Marilla and Matthew,
wanting to reduce their burdens a little.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:57.150
And since the orchard has gotten plenty of sunshine,

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:00.010
the apple harvest is large as usual.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:04.040
Anne works hard to pick
a lot in order to help Marilla.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.150
Oh yes!

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:20.530
That afternoon, on the suggestion of Marilla,

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:23.100
the three of them go to Bright River,

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:26.710
to do some winter shopping,
and to prepare apple juice.

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:30.200
This is the first time since
Anne came to Green Gables

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:32.240
that the three of them go out together.

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:33.960
Matthew, do you know what I think
you're thinking about?

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.260
Well, now...

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:38.510
That answer is rather obvious.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:42.110
But you definitely do not know
what I'm thinking about.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:45.800
Nonsense, Matthew and you
must be thinking about the same thing.

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:52.510
That's true. But I also remembered the day
one year after I came to Green Gables.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:59.890
I remember that you had Matthew take
me through the White Way of Delight.

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:03.800
Well, now... That's what happened.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.390
Yes.

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:43.250
Oh, what a wonderful smell!

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:47.740
Take this bottle to Charlottetown.

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:51.270
Oh! With this much,
I can give some to everyone.

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:56.700
Matthew, what do you think of this?

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:59.140
Well, now...

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:03.320
But don't you think this one is better?

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.320
Autumn days are short.

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:10.260
Anne, Matthew, and Marilla

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:16.170
all keenly feel great joy at being alive.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.550
Dolly. When we meet next week,

00:20:35.550 --> 00:20:37.680
you will have been jumping
all about the place, right?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:40.330
Anne, you'll be late
if you don't hurry up!

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:41.410
Coming!

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.330
Well, take care.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.340
I'm leaving.

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:59.710
It's getting colder now,
so take care not to catch a cold.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:01.140
You two take care, too.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:04.250
Don't worry about us.

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:05.120
Go now.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:38.320
Take care, Anne.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:39.880
You, too, Diana.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:41.760
Please try to get that scholarship.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.190
I will.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:46.730
I couldn't tell Matthew and Marilla after all.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.490
You said that Anne wants to go to college?

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:54.630
You didn't know? Even I know about it.

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:56.400
Where did you hear about this?

00:21:56.510 --> 00:21:59.500
Well, Ruby was very sure about it.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:04.530
Anne looked different whenever Josie
talked about the scholarship.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:12.450
It's not a good thing to send them to town, after all.

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:15.250
Only one year away from home,

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:17.150
and because she's good at studying,

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:19.340
she decides to go to university without your permission.

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:22.400
That's not what a loving daughter should do.

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:27.270
Matthew has had many seizures lately, right?

00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:31.830
Don't you think she should come back
home and become a teacher at the school?

00:22:36.070 --> 00:22:37.200
Rachel.

00:22:39.520 --> 00:22:43.480
Do you know why we still have
not adopted Anne officially?

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:48.550
That child was bestowed upon us by God.

00:22:48.590 --> 00:22:50.720
She doesn't belong to us.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:54.990
If that's what she wants to do,
I will allow her to do it.

00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:02.090
Forgive me...

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:07.590
And if she can get the scholarship,

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:11.250
she can go to college
by her self?

00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:16.340
This is a great honor,
and if the school fees are paid for,

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:20.320
even her real parents wouldn't be
silly enough to discourage her.

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:22.090
Marilla...

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:26.500
Anne must have thought of us,
and decided not to tell us.

00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:32.180
We don't know if she can get that scholarship.

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:37.250
I will write to her and tell her
she may advance towards that goal.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:41.370
Well, well. You've changed a lot, too.

00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:46.860
Anne will probably continue to
surprise you in the future.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:48.570
I'll take one.

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:22.440
Anne has decided to stay in Charlottetown
to prepare for the final exam,

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:25.050
but then she finds out that Matthew
has collapsed due to a seizure.

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:27.810
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 44

00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:29.800
Winter at Queen's

00:24:29.890 --> 00:24:31.290
Please look forward to it!
